Description: Drive interactive command-line REPLs and long-running interactive processes through tmux — send input, wait until the program is actually ready, and read its output back programmatically. Use whenever you need to interact with a running interactive process rather than run a one-shot command: a Python/Node/psql/irb/sqlite REPL, an SSH session, a TUI, a debugger (gdb/pdb), or a nested `claude` session. Trigger phrases: "drive a REPL", "test in a tmux session", "interact with a running interactive process", "feed input to a process on stdin", "automate a CLI that prompts", "send-keys / capture-pane". Covers tmux send-keys (and the literal-text vs Enter/C-m gotcha), capture-pane reads, a wait_for_prompt readiness poller, and session lifecycle (new-session/new-window/detach/kill-session). NOT for one-shot non-interactive shell commands — run those directly with the Bash tool; reach for this only when a process stays open and exchanges input/output across multiple steps.
